1
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:26,000
"Blue Collar" is the American Dream. If you're rich, you can buy
it. If you're anything else, you gotta fight for it.

2
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:46,000
Blue Collar is a drama, crime film directed by Paul Schrader.

3
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:06,000
Fed up with mistreatment at the hands of both management and union brass, and coupled with financial hardships on
each man's end, three auto assembly line workers hatch a plan to rob a safe at union headquarters.

4
00:25:20,000 --> 00:25:26,000
Ezekiel 'Zeke' Brown, played by Richard Pryor.

5
00:31:40,000 --> 00:31:46,000
Jerry Bartowski, played by Harvey Keitel.

6
00:38:00,000 --> 00:38:06,000
Sam 'Smokey' James, played by Yaphet Kotto.

7
00:44:20,000 --> 00:44:26,000
Bobby Joe, played by Ed Begley Jr..

8
00:50:40,000 --> 00:50:46,000
Eddie Johnson, played by Harry Bellaver.

9
00:57:00,000 --> 00:57:06,000
Jenkins, played by George Memmoli.

10
01:03:20,000 --> 01:03:26,000
Blue Collar is a 1978 American crime drama film directed
by Paul Schrader in his directorial debut.

11
01:09:40,000 --> 01:09:46,000
Written by Schrader and his brother Leonard, the film stars
Richard Pryor, Harvey Keitel and Yaphet Kotto.

12
01:16:00,000 --> 01:16:06,000
The film is both a critique of union practices and an
examination of life in a working-class Rust Belt enclave.

13
01:22:20,000 --> 01:22:26,000
Schrader, who wrote the script for Taxi Driver (1976), recalls the shooting as being very difficult because of
the artistic and personal tensions he had with the actors (including the stars themselves).

14
01:28:40,000 --> 01:28:46,000
Schrader has also stated that while making the film, he suffered an on-set
mental breakdown, which made him seriously reconsider his career.

15
01:35:00,000 --> 01:35:06,000
The film was shot in Detroit and Kalamazoo, Michigan.

16
01:41:20,000 --> 01:41:26,000
The film explores themes of factory worker, robbery, blackmail, drinking, union.

17
01:47:40,000 --> 01:47:46,000
The tone is emotional.
